If you're encountering large mimics by the time you still have 10 max
HP, I'd like to know how you're doing it!

As someone else said, you get 3-4 turns for every turn the mimic gets,
which is usually plenty of time to write a successful dust-E even if
you do it one word at a time.
Semi-permanent engraving only has two uses in my experience:  if you
can do it fast (/oDig, Athame, Marker in a pinch) it's guaranteed to
be correct, and last at least 1 turn, usually far more; or if you're
on an empty level and you want to put down an E on your stash square
but don't have a lightning / fire wand.

In pretty much every other case I can think of, dust-E is better than
engraving.  The trick is not to disturb the E once it's worked by
fighting on that square immediately after.  Either rest (.) which has
a better chance of keeping it intact, or run away and write more E
further away from the threat.


